+- The key [羊](羊.md), "sheep," is at the top, and [我](我.md), "self; I; ego," is below it. [議](議.md), "deliberate; debate," and [儀](儀.md), "ceremony; formal conduct," both contain 義 at the right and are also read ギ, as are [疑](疑.md), "doubt; suspect," and [技](技.md), "skill; technique." [養](養.md), "nourish; raise; adopt," has the same 羊 at the top. All are different kanji.
 - [役](役.md), "role; duty," and [務](務.md), "duties," overlap the sense "duty" that 義 and 義務 carry, and [意](意.md), "meaning, intention," overlaps "meaning." [正](正.md), "correct, proper," and [敬](敬.md), "respect; honor," overlap "right" and "honor," glosses of 正義 and 義理, and [理](理.md), "reason, logic," overlaps 道理 どうり, "reason; logic; sense; truth; right," and 条理 じょうり, "reason," which the Daijisen noun entry for ぎ lists as one sense of 義. [替](替.md), "replace; substitute," overlaps the stand-in sense of 義眼, 義歯 and 義足. They are kept out of this card's quiz options. Do not treat "duty," "meaning" or "right" as exclusive to any one character.
 
